  <!-- ════════ §C — TWO QUESTIONS, ONE FROM EACH SHORE ════════ -->
  <section class="sb-section" id="sharp">
    <div class="sb-eyebrow">The two questions</div>
    <h2 class="sb-h2">Why not simply own bitcoin? And why not simply hold Treasuries?</h2>
    <p class="sb-lead">STRC sits between two things a holder could otherwise own outright &mdash; bitcoin on one shore, a Treasury on the other. Each shore has its question. If the case for STRC is &ldquo;wait for bitcoin to recover and the price returns to par,&rdquo; then the below-par bull case and the bitcoin bull case are <strong>the same bet with different payoff shapes</strong> &mdash; so why not own bitcoin? And if the case is a steady cash yield, a Treasury already pays one without the issuer or bitcoin risk &mdash; so why STRC? The table answers both, cell by cell. The bitcoin column is the live arithmetic from <a href="/discount-or-premium">Discount, or Premium?</a>; the Treasury column reuses the parent page&rsquo;s 10-year yield.</p>

