  <section class="sb-section" id="record">
    <div class="sb-eyebrow">STRC&rsquo;s own short record</div>
    <h2 class="sb-h2">Price against par, since issuance</h2>
    <p class="sb-lead">The lens, run over the instrument&rsquo;s whole history. What it shows: the peg held for months, then broke with bitcoin&rsquo;s drawdown &mdash; par is a magnet in calm and an aspiration in stress, on the evidence so far.</p>

    <div class="sb-record" id="sbRecordStrip" aria-label="STRC price against par, schematic since issuance"></div>
    <p class="sb-record-cap" id="sbRecordCap">A schematic of shape, not tick data &mdash; anchored to the known points (issuance near par, the all-time high, the all-time low, and today) and annotated with the rate changes and issuer actions along the way.</p>
    <p class="sb-note"><strong>The record is short &mdash; about one year.</strong> That is itself a risk disclosure, not a footnote: there is not yet enough history to know how STRC behaves across a full bitcoin cycle, and the floor that has held so far is evidence, not law. No instrument like this has existed before, and the entire record is one bitcoin drawdown &mdash; how STRC trades through a bull leg is unobserved, and cycles between discount and premium are plausible and untested.</p>
  </section>

